 ### Done
+- **Speed S4-W (2026-11-15, SPEED-3, the Prize Wheel's result card on the GBA, speed audit 2 / S2-4b follow-up; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 3: S4-W", ledger row S4-W):** the spin goes straight into a held result card (S2-1's modal hold): a held tick draws only the bulbs, the winning icon's light, the hub and the pointer; the confetti, stars and puffs keep what is under them per page (`plat_under`, `mg_fx_walk`), the window's pop is painted over a clean ring, the hint over its clean rows, stars stop at the window's edge. GBA drawn fps (libmgba, `speed2_fair.txt`, before -> after): spin window 29.9 (one 67 ms frame) -> **30.0 (2:130)**, result card (60 ticks: pop, confetti, stars) 15.0 -> **30.5 (2:60)**, card held 15.0 -> **30.1 (4.2 ms a tick)**, done 30.0 -> 30.0. A curse (shake, flash, puffs) keeps 13 frames over 33 ms (was 26): result 16.7 -> 23.7 fps, its held card 15.1 -> 30.1. The disc outside the window is the full frame's pixel for pixel on every tick; the trades (the held card's sway, twinkle, glint and bob stand still; stars, line and hint 2-5 ticks late at the result; the pop's way back at full size; stars cut at the window) are in the docs. No static RAM (`.bss` 254,828 B, the scene scratch claim +8,858 B while the wheel runs); PS1 compiled out (`_end` 0x801e0420, 130,000 B below the stack top, the base's); Dreamcast has no hold (full frame, 30). New `modal_hold_fair_wheel_result_card` (six seeds, hold on and off, native two-page hold `nat_hold_pages`). **Still short:** a curse's first ~0.9 s (shake and flash are full frames).
 - **Speed S2-4c (2026-11-15, the kitchen on the GBA, speed audit 2 causes C3 / C1, audit 3 rank 12, partial; measured on libmgba, PCSX-Redux and Flycast on `5aa25cd1` and again on `366ee6c1`, `9dc5e39a`, `e587f9c1`, `167c08ba` (with S2-4b), `262bf2b7` (with S3-2) and the tip it landed on, `fe410024`; docs/GBA.md "Speed wave 2: S2-4c", ledger row 59, docs/PS1.md "Speed tour 2"):** the kitchen's wall, jars and counter (and, for the recipe book, the window, the book and the doily) are kept pictures baked into the GBA ROM (`DOOMO_BACKDROP_KITCHEN`), and every screen (the book, the cooking steps, the result card, the counter) is drawn as layers of SP7's retained stage, each redrawn only when its key or box changes or a changed box lies on it; Granny's 164 poses are baked too (`runner --bake-poses`, `plat_cook_pose`, the file read by `cook_pose_find`: one image instead of ~45 ellipses), cut off where the counter covers her; faces are blitted above the counter only, bubbles are two layers, boxes and keys are measured and follow the translated text; `stage_rows` copies short spans by DMA (the fair's S2-4b windows hash the same, tick for tick). All exact (`test_cook_kept`: the kitchen with the stage on / off, 5,140 frames at each of two sizes, day and night, and in Spanish, identical; the baked pose file read back and checked pose by pose; GBA `vhash-seq` against the tip: 13 windows identical, Spanish 2,479 of 2,480 frames (the tip's one differing frame is the same picture one pixel lower), the counter's windows differ only inside the faces). GBA drawn fps: recipe book 20.0 -> **30.0**, chop 21.9 -> **30.0**, fry 19.8 -> **30.0** (every frame two vblanks); stir 20.0 -> 30.0, bake 20.8 -> 29.9, simmer 21.8 -> 29.7 (one or two 50-67 ms frames at a step change); result card 15.0 -> 20.8 (21.1 before S2-4b's stage changes); with S3-2's portrait jobs counter 26.3 -> 29.2 and serving 24.3 -> 29.3 (3-6 frames of 50 ms a window); `expect-fps` floors. The approved 15 Hz trades were measured on the result card and save nothing over a kept picture (21.1 fps either way: each Mode 4 page is two ticks old), so none is taken. GBA EWRAM and IWRAM unchanged, ROM +320 KB (three pictures, the poses). PS1: compiled out, `_end` unchanged (130,000 B below the stack top with the FMV on `fe410024`, the tip's; delta 0 measured on every earlier tip), the kitchen's table the tip's. Dreamcast: all 16 windows 30.0. **Still short (open):** the result card (needs G2-EX's clipped redraw), the counter / serving's three-vblank frames (animated faces, bobbing bubbles), the step-change frames of stir, bake and simmer; on the PS1 the result card's, counter's and serving's single 50 ms frames (unlock grants, faces: S3-2).
 - **Talk TKP0-MEASURE (2026-11-15, TALK round 13; docs/design/talk/TKP_PLAN.md, docs/TALK.md 6q):** the PS1 re-measure and a buildable plan, no resident byte. Talk linked on the PS1: 146 KB of files (92 KB as one new overlay group, 0 B of slot growth; resident +19,520 B with the group alone, +15,616 B with the typed line off, about 2 to 4 KB after the planned clean-ups, inside the 12 KB share). PS1 subset of TALK_en.BIN 577,786 B against the 319,488 B budget (9,062 alternatives); lossless levers (word-token strings, packed rows) reach about 437 KB, which does not fit: CR10's part store holds SPU RAM 0x50000-0x7DFFF, leaving Talk 278,528 B at most (decision D1 for the owner: a PS1 content tier, or drop Talk on the PS1). Measured: 2,075 database reads and 43.4 KB a line (74 KB an exchange), 661,000 instructions a line (48 % the lint probes); estimated R3000 step 12 to 30 ms typical, so the generator must be sliced. First load estimated 1.4 to 1.6 s against the 1.5 s gate. Packages TKP1 to TKP6 with acceptance tests. New tools `ps1/tools/talk_size.sh`, `core/tools/talk_reads.sh`, `core/tools/talk_steps.sh`. PS1 margin 110,560 B on the rebased tree (unchanged), GBA sizes unchanged.
