+### Speed wave 3: S4-W, the Prize Wheel's result card as a held picture (2026-11-15)
+
+The Wheel of Fate's spin was held at 30 by S2-3, but its result card ran at 15 fps for as long as it stood (60 ms a tick:
+the whole tent, host, disc and speech bubble drawn again under the confetti), and the first tick of the card was one
+67 ms frame in the spin window. S2-4b's Done line said "its disc as a kept picture is next". The disc cannot be baked
+into the ROM like the kitchen (its angle is the spin's, any of 4,096), and while the card stands the disc is still: so
+the card is a **held frame** (S2-1's `ui_modal_hold`, the two Mode 4 pages both carry the picture) and a held tick
+draws only what changes.
+
+**What a held tick of the card draws** (`core/src/mg_wheel.c`, `wh_result_tick`): the 20 bulbs (one colour for all,
+every third tick), the winning icon's white disc (every fourth tick), the hub's eyelid and the pointer's flapper. For
+the last three a full frame keeps the clean pixels under them (new `plat_under` in `plat_ext.h`: `PLAT_UNDER_GET` /
+`PUT` of a small box, `PLAT_UNDER_PAGE` which of the two pages is drawn on; the GBA copies halfwords, `gba/src/hold.c`,
+no RAM) and a held tick puts them back before it draws. Everything else the card has comes and goes **over** the held
+pages and is put back the same way:
+
+* the **confetti, stars and puffs** keep what is under each particle, a list for each page (a held tick draws on the
+  page of two ticks ago): `mg_fx_walk` (mg_fx.c) gives each live particle's box (rounded out to even x and width) to
+  `wh_keep_save`, which keeps it before the particle is drawn; the next tick on that page puts the lists back, newest
+  first. A full frame that starts a hold with particles up copies its list to the other page (the platform copies the
+  picture). 40 particles, 1,024 B a page; more, or a kind with no box (hearts, drops ...), is a full frame.
+* the **window's pop** (12 ticks, overshooting to 300/256) is painted over a clean copy of the ring round the window
+  (four boxes, 3,936 B at 240x160), taken once the card's other parts are on both pages; the overshoot's way back is
+  drawn at the full size (see the trades). The finished card (window, title, texts, hint) is painted on two ticks,
+  one for each page, then not again.
+* the **speech line, Wagerine's face and the hint** change at the result: two held ticks each (one for each page) as in
+  S2-3, after the two ticks that draw the whole disc on both pages (the disc is new: the spin's last tick moved it).
+  The hint's pill changes width, so the clean rows under both pills (up to 2,048 B) are kept in a full frame.
+* the **stars** stop at the window's edge (they pass behind it on a full frame: `mg_fx_exclude`, two boxes, the
+  window and the title pill; `fx_sparkle` is `ui_sparkle`'s shape cut by them), so a star falling over the window does
+  not end the hold.
+
+Where the memory is: the wheel claims 8,858 B more of the **scene scratch** (the 12 KB claim, `WhKeep`: 2,560 + 8,858 = 11,418 B; the same
+block the Derby's racers use), no static RAM: `.bss` 254,828 B and the IWRAM groups (room 9,800 B, UI 10,124 B) are
+what they were, ledger row S4-W. The PS1 compiles all of it out (`WH_KEEPS`, no held frame there): `_end`
+0x801e0420, 130,000 B below the stack top with the boot FMV, the base's, and the minigame group the same size. The native
+platform's hold gained `nat_hold_pages(1)` (two pages like the GBA; default one picture as before) for the test.
+
+**Trades (GBA only, pixel-changing; before / after shots: `evidence/S4-W/before_after_result_ticks_*.png` in the
+builder's scratchpad, the diff in the third column):**
+1. A held card stands still, as the held spin does (S2-3): the tent's sway, the sparkles' twinkle, the host frame's
+   bob and the window's glint (a few hundred pixels a tick, a few pixels in the window).
+2. The result's first two ticks draw the whole disc on both pages and nothing else: the stars show 2 ticks (66 ms)
+   late, the speech line and the hint 2-3 ticks late, the face 4-5 (it was 1 tick of 60 ms before).
+3. The window's way back from its overshoot (ticks 8-11 of the pop, 250/244/249/254 of 256) is drawn at 256: up to 6 px
+   wider than the bounce, for 4 ticks; its way up (ticks 1-5) is the same pixels.
+4. A star over the window is cut at the window's edge: its pixels in the 2-3 px of the window's drop shadow are not
+   shaded as on a full frame.
+5. Not changed: the disc, the bulbs, the winner's light, the hub and the pointer, the rim and its shadow are the full
+   frame's, pixel for pixel, on all 220 ticks of the probe (`vhash-seq` frames of the spin's end, the pop, the confetti
+   and the held card against the base's ROM, the disc and rim outside the window compared by script: 0 pixels differ on
+   219 ticks, 32 on the tick that shows the star 2 ticks late) and in `modal_hold_fair_wheel_result_card` (six seeds,
+   hold on and off, 900 ticks each, on the native platform holding on two pages).
